      rationale: "A falling level of consciousness with a new [[anisocoria|unilateral dilated pupil]] in a patient with a swelling infarct means [[uncal-herniation|herniation]] until proved otherwise. Airway and ventilation come first, because hypoxia and hypercapnia raise ICP and an obstructed airway will kill sooner. Positioning, freeing venous drainage, [[hyperosmolar-therapy|osmotherapy]], and, if needed, brief hyperventilation lower ICP within minutes and buy time. Imaging and neurosurgical review for [[decompressive-craniectomy|decompressive craniectomy]] proceed together. Hyperventilation is not continued, because it reduces cerebral blood flow.",
