      presentation: "cerebellar-hemorrhage-respiratory-arrest",
      usage: ["review"],
      vignette: "A 71-year-old with hypertension develops sudden occipital headache, vomiting, and inability to stand. CT shows a large right cerebellar hemorrhage compressing the fourth ventricle. Over the next hour he becomes drowsy, his neck becomes stiff, his breathing turns irregular, and then it stops.",
